# Monorepo Package & Dependency Management — Cursor Adapter

**Applies to:** All packages in `packages/*` and apps consuming them

Use the repository's canonical shared guidance instead of duplicating
package/dependency rules in this Cursor-specific file:

1. Read [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) § Monorepo Package Rules — canonical
   source for exports, `dist/` output, `workspace:*` dependencies, and build
   wiring.
2. See [`.agents/rules/03-monorepo-packages.mdc`](../../.agents/rules/03-monorepo-packages.mdc)
   for the same key rules in house-rule form.
3. For package extraction and multi-consumer boundary decisions, load
   [`package-extraction-strategy`](../../.agents/skills/package-extraction-strategy/SKILL.md).
4. For a detailed worked reference (package.json, tsconfig, Vite, Turbo
   examples), see `.claude/memory/monorepo-package-rules.md` — the examples
   there follow the same canonical rules and apply regardless of tool.

`AGENTS.md` and `.agents/rules/` are authoritative. Keep this file as a
routing adapter so Cursor cannot retain a stale copy of those rules.
